lexical.evidence_text:
It is prohibited to fuel and/or refuel an Automobile in Pit Lane during practice, qualifying or a race.

Unless otherwise approved by the TD , an Automobile is only permitted to be drained of fuel and/or refueled whilst in its designated garage bay; using the 'Fill and Drain' dry break fitting and a fit for purpose closed- circuit fueling system manufactured by a specialist company.

When an Automobile is being drained of fuel or refueled:

The Automobile's engine must be switched off;

The Automobile and all equipment must be grounded to earth;

At least one (1) Team member must be designated as a fire attendant and in possession of at least one (1) certified and fully functioning 4.5 kg dry powder fire extinguisher;

The designated fire attendant must not perform any other task during the procedure;

A drip/catch mat/tray capable of containing any spillage must be positioned below the refueling point of the Automobile .

